[h1]0.10 The Ox Paradox[/h1]
For EU5 1.4.5, with or without the Across the Pillars DLC. A major update and not save compatible: please start a new campaign.

Full patch notes: [url=https://github.com/JanB1989/prosper-or-perish-constructor/releases/tag/0.10.0]0.10 The Ox Paradox on GitHub[/url]

[h2]Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*] Local food: no more food market. Every province lives off its own food store, and the months in store drive growth.
[*] New food buildings: Tavern, Cookshop, Grange, a reworked Victualling Yard and bigger Granaries. Victuals are the only food traded between provinces.
[*] Arable Land: population capacity is the land that feeds people. Land improvements win land, farms take it.
[*] Navigable Rivers: fleets sail the great rivers far inland, and their banks hold ports and shipyards.
[*] A new map underneath: climates, vegetation, terrain, soils, fertility and redrawn rivers.
[*] Eight crop farms with four tiers, Manual Labor as a good, manufacturing tiers and town rights.
[*] Logistics: building past a location's supported levels costs market access; logistics buildings win it back.
[*] Smarter AI: it builds by prices and shortages, takes connected land in peace deals and plans more wars.
[*] A rewritten, illustrated Europedia.
[/list]

[h2]Two Example Games[/h2]
Two full observer games on this release, 1337 to 1837, with map videos and charts:
[list]
[*] [url=https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-preview/runs/060ad1de_995b_4913_92b1_5eeec0366bc5/]Game 1[/url]: 1.24 billion people in 1837. The Ming unite China and hold it to the end.
[*] [url=https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-preview/runs/af7dce96_68e1_4bb2_b21d_b272802c9c05/]Game 2[/url]: 1.29 billion people in 1837. China stays split, the Ottomans become the largest realm and Brandenburg becomes Prussia.
[/list]

[h2]Keep Playing an Older Version[/h2]
To finish a running campaign on an older version, download it from the [url=https://github.com/JanB1989/prosper-or-perish-constructor/releases]GitHub releases page[/url], unzip it, and copy the folder [i]Prosper or Perish (Population Growth & Food Rework)[/i] into your EU5 mod folder, usually here:
C:\Users\YourUserName\Documents\Paradox Interactive\Europa Universalis V\mod

